    <bpmn:process id="W_W5366" name="W5366. Take-Back Program Incident, Spill/Leak &amp; Exposure Response" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Spill/leak (oil/paint/acid/mercury), battery thermal event, or customer/staff exposure at a take-back point
Frequency: Uncommon (~20–80 incidents/yr group-wide, per the Volume register); high severity
Volume: ~20–80 incidents/yr group-wide
Owner: HSE Officer
Participants: Store Manager, Compliance Specialist, BFP, DENR-EMB (if reportable), Medical (VS-83)
Source: workflow W5366 — Take-Back Program Incident, Spill/Leak &amp; Exposure Response</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5366_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5366_Lane1" name="HSE Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5366_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5366_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5366_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5366_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5366_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5366_Lane2" name="Compliance Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5366_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5366_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5366_Start4" name="Spill/leak (oil/paint/acid/mercury), battery thermal event, or customer/staff exposure at…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5366_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5366_Task5" name="Secure the area, contain the spill with the spill kit, and evacuate/exclude…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Secure the area, contain the spill with the spill kit, and evacuate/exclude customers; render first aid/exposure care.
Responsible (R): HSE Officer
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5366_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5366_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5366_Task6" name="Identify the substance (mercury, acid, oil, solvent) and apply the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Identify the substance (mercury, acid, oil, solvent) and apply the substance-specific response (e.g. mercury vapor procedure for broken lamps — W5356).
Responsible (R): HSE Officer
Accountable (A): HSE Officer
Duration: immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5366_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5366_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5366_Task7" name="Notify BFP/DENR-EMB if reportable (significant spill, mercury release, fire)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Notify BFP/DENR-EMB if reportable (significant spill, mercury release, fire); notify insurance (VS-26).
Responsible (R): Compliance Specialist
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: within SLA</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5366_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5366_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5366_Task8" name="Clean up, dispose of contaminated material via the licensed TSD (W5360), and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Clean up, dispose of contaminated material via the licensed TSD (W5360), and decontaminate the area.
Responsible (R): HSE Officer
Accountable (A): HSE Officer
Duration: per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5366_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5366_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5366_Task9" name="Root-cause and corrective action (containment design, staff training, policy)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Root-cause and corrective action (containment design, staff training, policy); capture lessons-learned (VS-133).
Responsible (R): HSE Officer
Accountable (A): Compliance Specialist
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5366_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5366_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5366_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5366_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5366_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-793 (ensure controlled execution — Recovery, Disposal, Compliance Reporting &amp; Stewardship Analytics (PA-187.3).) | - operational: spill kits + substance procedures at every point.
Owner: HSE Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
